[0.1.9]
* Update LibreCrawl to commit 789c236, which forces UTF-8 output so redirected logs no longer crash on Windows.

[0.1.8]
* Update LibreCrawl to commit f25bee6 with indexability, inlinks and Link Score, sitemap audit, and saved crawl comparison.

[0.1.7]
* Update LibreCrawl to commit b5b288f, which fixes accounts stuck unverified when email is not configured.

[0.1.6]
* Update LibreCrawl to commit 38e3bb4 with n-gram analysis and export, table column visibility and sorting, and saved column preferences.

[0.1.5]
* Update LibreCrawl to commit 8f4d31d with custom CSS/XPath extraction and list-mode crawls.
* Cache robots.txt per host and show the failure reason when a crawl cannot start.

[0.1.4]
* Update LibreCrawl to commit 5ae2792.
* Honour the configured crawl delay with JavaScript rendering disabled.
* Fix saving and loading large crawl files and improve large-site link bookkeeping performance.

[0.1.3]
* The Community Apps Package link now opens this repository. The listing builds that link from packagerUrl, so the 0.1.2 packageUrl change had no visible effect.
* No change to the app; LibreCrawl stays at commit 05a1372.

[0.1.2]
* Link the Community Apps Package button to this package's repository.
* Requires Cloudron 10.0.0 or later; Cloudron 9 servers can no longer read this catalog.
* No change to the app; LibreCrawl stays at commit 05a1372.

[0.1.1]
* Security update: move to the digest-pinned Cloudron base image 6.0.1 with its patched CA bundle and shared MIME data. LibreCrawl stays at commit 05a1372.

[0.1.0]
* Initial Cloudron package for LibreCrawl commit 05a1372.
* Signed-in-only access with operator-managed accounts and persistent sessions.
* Persistent SQLite data, upgrade snapshots and daily finished-crawl retention.
* Chromium rendering available, disabled by default; 2 GiB default memory.
